NAME
       info - read documentation in Info format

SYNOPSIS
       info [TOPIC]

DESCRIPTION
       info reads the GNU project's manuals, which are written as Info
       documents: long, book-like texts split into nodes joined by menus and
       links. The Info manual of a GNU tool (coreutils, bash, sed, grep, tar)
       is often fuller than its man page and has more examples. With no
       TOPIC, info opens the directory node, a menu of every Info manual.

       Moving around in the real info reader: Space and Backspace page,
       Tab jumps to the next link, Enter follows it, n and p go to the next
       and previous node, u goes up, l goes back, s searches, q quits. When a
       topic has no Info manual, info shows its man page instead. The pinfo
       program (not installed by default) is a friendlier reader.

       Cert Lab shows the topic's manual page under info.

EXAMPLES
              $ info
              $ info ls
              $ info coreutils

FILES
       /usr/share/info
              The installed Info documents.

SEE ALSO
       man(1), /usr/share/doc
